    "result_text": "All clean \u2014 the only remaining mentions are an intentional explanatory javadoc and the test's own assertion that the old fields are gone.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`); the audit stream now emits e.g. `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.\n\n**What `memberId` is composed of** (verified against the test's independent oracles):\n- `REGION` \u2014 resolved from postcode\u2192city\u2192`UNKNOWN` (`NSW`)\n- `FY` \u2014 2-digit fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted registration date (`27`)\n- `HASH8` \u2014 first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (`16E6609E`) \u2014 same hash the test recomputes\n- `CHK` \u2014 one Luhn digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>` (`1`)\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`Owner`** \u2014 replaced `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` fields+accessors with `memberId`; removed `getCheckDigit()`; added static `regionSegment`/`fiscalYearSegment` parsers; `getFiscalYear()` now reads the FY segment from the memberId (falling back to the registration-date computation), keeping it in lock-step with the identity.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 `saveOwner` now generates one `memberId` on create; collision de-dup (`-<n>`) applies to the memberId; the human audit line and the structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` (JSON field renamed to `memberId`) and `primaryIdentifier` all reference the memberId. Replaced the old generators with `generateMemberId`/`deduplicateMemberId`/`memberHash`/`luhnCheckDigit`.\n- **`OwnerMapper.toLocality`** \u2014 now derives the REGION from the memberId, so `ownerSegment` (which depends on locality) references the memberId.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`; added the read-only `memberId` property.\n- **schema.sql** (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres) \u2014 dropped `customer_code`/`membership_number` columns, added `member_id`.\n\nOne interpretation call worth flagging: the spec's \"the fiscal-year value \u2026 must reference the memberId\" \u2014 I read this as deriving `fiscalYear` (and `locality`) from the stored memberId segments, mirroring how locality previously read the customerCode. Since the FY embedded in the memberId is computed from the same registration date, the reported value is identical either way; parsing it from the memberId just guarantees they can't drift.",
