    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, idiomatic unification. Structurally:\n\n- **Parsing vs. generation split is coherent.** The format-decoding helpers (`regionSegment`, `fiscalYearSegment`) live as static methods on `Owner`, sitting naturally alongside the existing `fiscalYearOf` format helper, while the id *construction* (`generateMemberId`, `memberHash`, `luhnCheckDigit`, `deduplicateMemberId`) stays in `ClinicServiceImpl` where it belongs \u2014 generation needs the repository for collision handling, so it can't move to the entity. This mirrors the pre-existing split (construction in service, locality parsing near the model).\n- **`OwnerMapper.toLocality` is improved, not just patched.** The old inline `indexOf('-')` substring parsing is replaced by delegation to `Owner.regionSegment(...)`, so the region-extraction logic now has a single home and is reused by both the mapper and `getFiscalYear`.\n- **No duplication introduced.** The removed `Owner.getCheckDigit()` Luhn loop reappears exactly once, as `luhnCheckDigit` in the service \u2014 there is no second Luhn implementation. Grep confirms no stray `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`/`customerHash` references survive except the one intentional explanatory doc comment.\n- **`getFiscalYear` prefers the memberId segment with a registrationDate fallback**, keeping the reported value and the embedded FY in lock-step while reusing `fiscalYearSegment` and `fiscalYearOf` rather than re-deriving anything.\n- Renames (`customerHash`\u2192`memberHash`, `deduplicateCustomerCode`\u2192`deduplicateMemberId`), the audit record field, the `primaryIdentifier` single-source-of-truth method, schema columns, and the OpenAPI schema all move together consistently.\n\nNothing is becoming a catch-all and the logic sits in the units a maintainer of this codebase would expect.",
